# Trade Events

## Purpose

This chapter defines the canonical events governing the proposal, negotiation, execution, modification, cancellation, and completion of trades within a League.

Unlike Drafts or Free Agency, Trades are multi-asset transactions between two or more Franchises. A single Trade may involve Players, Contracts, Draft Picks, salary considerations, or future conditional assets.

The Trade itself is not the movement of assets.

The Trade authorizes the movement of assets.

Ownership changes occur through the events emitted during Trade execution.

---

# Guiding Principle

Trades negotiate intent.

Trade execution moves assets.

Ownership changes through ownership events.

Financial changes through contract events.

A Trade coordinates multiple state changes but owns none of them directly.

---

# Trade Model

```text
Trade
      │
contains
      ▼
Trade Assets
      │
may reference
      ├───────────────┐
      ▼               ▼
Player         Draft Pick
      │               │
      └──────┬────────┘
             ▼
       Trade Executed
             │
             ▼
Ownership Events

Financial Events
```

A Trade is a coordination aggregate.

The Trade itself never owns Players, Contracts, or Draft Picks.

It references them.

---

# Trade Lifecycle

```text
TradeProposed
        │
        ▼
TradeModified (optional)
        │
        ▼
TradeAccepted
        │
        ▼
TradeValidated
        │
        ▼
TradeExecuted
        │
        ▼
TradeCompleted
```

Alternative paths:

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeRejected
```

or

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeCancelled
```

or

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeExpired
```

---

# Scope

This chapter defines:

- TradeProposed
- TradeModified
- TradeAccepted
- TradeRejected
- TradeCancelled
- TradeExpired
- TradeValidated
- TradeExecutionStarted
- TradeExecuted
- TradeCompleted
- TradeExecutionFailed

---

# General Invariants

Every Trade shall satisfy:

1. Every Trade has at least two participating Franchises.
2. Every Trade Asset belongs to exactly one Franchise prior to execution.
3. Every Trade Asset may appear only once within a Trade.
4. Trades must satisfy League Rules before execution.
5. Trade validation precedes execution.
6. Trade execution is atomic.
7. Either every asset moves or none do.
8. Historical Trades are immutable.
9. Trade execution never directly edits historical events.
10. Asset ownership changes are emitted by their owning aggregates.

---

# TradeProposed

## Purpose

Represents the creation of a proposed Trade between participating Franchises.

### Trigger

A Franchise submits a Trade offer.

### Business Impact

• Creates pending Trade

• Locks proposal snapshot

• Enables negotiation

• Starts Trade lifecycle

• AI evaluates fairness

### AI Interpretation

The AI may immediately evaluate:

- Fairness
- Cap implications
- Competitive balance
- Risk
- Future value

without affecting League state.

---

# TradeModified

## Purpose

Represents modification of a pending Trade proposal before acceptance.

### Business Impact

• Updates Trade Assets

• Resets validation

• Invalidates previous evaluations

• Requires new AI analysis

---

# TradeAccepted

## Purpose

Represents agreement by all required parties.

### Business Impact

• Locks Trade contents

• Enables validation

• Prevents unauthorized modification

---

# TradeRejected

## Purpose

Represents explicit rejection of a Trade proposal.

### Business Impact

• Ends negotiation

• Releases proposal

• No asset movement occurs

---

# TradeCancelled

## Purpose

Represents withdrawal of a pending Trade before execution.

### Business Impact

• Terminates proposal

• Releases Trade

• Restores negotiation freedom

---

# TradeExpired

## Purpose

Represents expiration of a Trade proposal due to time limits or League Rules.

### Business Impact

• Removes pending proposal

• Requires new Trade if negotiations continue

---

# TradeValidated

## Purpose

Represents successful verification that the proposed Trade satisfies all League Rules.

### Validation includes

- Salary Cap
- Roster Limits
- Contract Rules
- Draft Pick ownership
- Player ownership
- League restrictions

### Business Impact

• Confirms legality

• Authorizes execution

• Freezes validation state

---

# TradeExecutionStarted

## Purpose

Represents the beginning of atomic Trade execution.

### Business Impact

• Begins coordinated asset movement

• Prevents concurrent modification

• Creates execution transaction

---

# TradeExecuted

## Purpose

Represents successful execution of every asset movement authorized by the Trade.

### Business Impact

• Transfers Players

• Transfers Contracts

• Transfers Draft Picks

• Recalculates cap

• Recalculates roster state

• Recalculates League standings

• Invalidates franchise evaluations

• Invalidates League evaluations

### AI Interpretation

This is one of the highest-impact events in Legacy because multiple deterministic state changes occur simultaneously.

---

# TradeCompleted

## Purpose

Represents successful completion of every operation associated with Trade execution.

### Business Impact

• Finalizes Trade

• Releases execution locks

• Enables historical audit

• Enables downstream projections

---

# TradeExecutionFailed

## Purpose

Represents failure during Trade execution.

### Business Impact

• Rolls back partial execution

• Preserves previous ownership

• Preserves financial state

• Generates audit record

• Prevents inconsistent League state

---

# Workflow Examples

## Successful Trade

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeAccepted

↓

TradeValidated

↓

TradeExecutionStarted

↓

TradeExecuted

↓

TradeCompleted
```

---

## Rejected Trade

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeRejected
```

---

## Cancelled Trade

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeCancelled
```

---

## Failed Execution

```text
TradeProposed

↓

TradeAccepted

↓

TradeValidated

↓

TradeExecutionStarted

↓

TradeExecutionFailed
```

